  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Fort Wilderness Campground is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>People who already camp or travel with an RV</strong> and want a boat to Magic Kingdom, with hook-ups and internal buses on site.</li>
      <li><strong>Families who want the lowest full-price rate on property that still includes official Disney resort transportation.</strong> In 2026 a tent or pop-up site ran about $82 to $222 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups of up to eight</strong> who can live on a campsite and will use the trails, the marina and the Settlement.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You want a hotel room.</strong> There is no standard guest room on this page. The cabins are the furnished indoor option, and they have their own guide.</li>
      <li><strong>You dislike internal buses.</strong> Most trips, including the walk-up to the Magic Kingdom boat, start with a loop bus.</li>
      <li><strong>Your RV or tent will not fit the pad you booked.</strong> Official 2026 notes give concrete pad sizes by category. Read them before you assume a Premium Meadow site is just a better Preferred site.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="rooms">
    <h2>Site types, pad sizes and hook-ups</h2>
    <p>These are campsites. You bring the sleeping setup. Official 2026 listings say each category sleeps up to eight adults, with no extra-adult charge up to that limit. Sewage hook-up is listed on Full Hook-Up, Preferred, Premium and Premium Meadow sites, not on the tent or pop-up sites.</p>
